Bottom-up Progol Processor using MGTP (Prolog Version)
					Copyright (C) 1996 Koichi Furukawa

[Software]
source/progol.pl	PProgol main module
source/magic.pl		magic translation module
source/m2pl.pl		translation from MGTP to Prolog module
source/bot.pl		Construct MSH module
source/search.pl	Search through the subsumption lattice module

[Introduction]
This Software is an experimental system for inductive inference
written in Prolog.  It was developed for the purposes of parallelizing
Progol.

Instead of the original Progol's top-down computation, we employ
bottom-up computation to construct hypotheses.  MGTP(Model
Generation Theorem Prover) is used directly in this task.

The user can make an experiment on Machine Learning, and understand
Progol's mechanism. Since the software is written in Prolog and employ
MGTP, it has higher level of description and it is easier to
understand the whole system compared with the original Progol
written in C.

This software is a prototype of the parallel implementation. Therefore
the purpose of this system is to make the algorithm clear.  It will be
needed to modify and refine the system for efficient parallel
computation.

[Reference]
H.Fujita, K.Furukawa, N.Yagi, T.Ozaki :
Most Specific Hypothesis Generation in PROGOL by Using MGTP,
In the Proceedings of the 10th Annual Conference of JSAI,1996
(in Japanese)

N.Yagi, H.Fujita, T.Ozaki, K.Furukawa :
Note on Algorithm for Computing Heuristic Function of A*-search in PROGOL,
In the Proceedings of the 10th Annual Conference of JSAI,1996
(in Japanese)

H.Fujita, N.Yagi, T.Ozaki, K.Furukawa :
A New Design and Implementation of PROGOL by bottom-up computation,
In the Proceedings of the 6th International Workshop on Inductive Logic
Progoramming, also in the  Proceedings of the 25th SIG-FAI,1996
